WEBVTT

0
00:00:01.100 --> 00:00:07.980
Sprezzature is an AI engine for Design.
Figures draws the chart your rows ask for.

1
00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:13.712
A spreadsheet is open, and no chart
in it is obviously the right one.

2
00:00:13.800 --> 00:00:17.362
So you reach for the bar chart
you reached for last time.

3
00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:23.025
Ask an assistant instead. It writes
plotting code, and an image comes out.

4
00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:28.560
Nobody looks at that image. The labels
collide, on a white panel, on a dark page.

5
00:00:28.759 --> 00:00:32.821
Here you name the kind,
hand over your rows, and get a file back.

6
00:00:33.200 --> 00:00:38.640
167 kinds in 68 categories,
and every one of them is marked stable.

7
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:45.360
Exported, a chart is a picture.
Written line by line, it is a document.

8
00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:54.960
144 of the 167 generators share one root:
a title, a description, a dark twin.

9
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:03.350
Each kind declares the data roles it
needs, so your columns do the choosing.

10
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:08.320
Region, quarter and units fill 64
of the kinds, ranked by readability.

11
00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:14.920
All of that is deterministic,
and no model was consulted for any of it.

12
00:01:17.000 --> 00:01:21.875
So the Ralph Eyeball Loop renders it,
and a vision model looks at the picture.

13
00:01:22.000 --> 00:01:28.999
Qwen3-VL through Ollama, offline. What
it edits is the plan, never the picture.

14
00:01:29.560 --> 00:01:32.640
16 parts of this one take keyboard focus.

15
00:01:33.000 --> 00:01:37.250
Each one says its own numbers to a
reader who cannot see the ribbon.

16
00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:47.640
Go to sprezzature.ai,
and drop a GitHub star if it deserves it.

17
00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:52.440
Make it, audit it, take a look at it.
